, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to tap into"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to gain access to"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: I want to tap into this new market."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob02aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "market"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in business, an area or industry"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The clean eating market is getting larger."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob02aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "savvy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "experienced and knowledgeable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's a very savvy idea!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le03ob02aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Present Perfect Continuous vs Present Perfect"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The Present Perfect tense and the Present Perfect Continuous tense each has their own uses. You use both to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for an outline of the two tenses: "}, {"type": "example", "content": " I've been going to specialized cooking classes for two week."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Since you started as the manager, you've become attuned to the business side of the restaurant industry."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning/Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject + has/have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to talk about experience\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Since</span> you started as the manager, you've become attuned to the business side of the restaurant industry.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject + has/have + been v-ing \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to describe: <br> a single activity that lasts a long time OR <br> an action that is repeated over a long period of time  <br> <br> when a long activity has just stopped\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I've been going to specialized cooking classes <span class=\\\"strong\\\">for</span> two weeks.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To emphasize the <span class=\"strong\">action</span>, use the <span class=\"underline\">continuous</span> form. <br> <span class=\"italic\"> <li> They've been studying hard. </li></span></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To emphasize the <span class=\"strong\">result of the action</span>, use the <span class=\"underline\">simple</span> form. <br> <span class=\"italic\"> <li> I've won many cooking awards.</li></span></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li> You use FOR to talk about how long an action has been happening (a week, 2 days, five hours, two weeks etc.)</li> \t<li>You use SINCE to talk about when the action started (2010, Tuesday, I started</li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have you been losing weight?"},